# =============================================================================
# paper/ and presentations/ generated figures
# =============================================================================
# Only track what the document actually embeds, in the ONE format each
# consumes (paper/main.tex wants PDF; presentation.qmd wants SVG, for
# Quarto/reveal.js) -- scripts/make_figures.py's own local convention is
# to always write PDF+SVG together for both --mode paper/presentation,
# so plenty of untracked files accumulate here that were never meant to
# be committed. Add a new `!path` line below whenever a new figure gets
# embedded in main.tex/presentation.qmd; remove one when a figure is
# dropped from the document. A figure under active hand-editing (e.g.
# Inkscape touch-ups) can add its OTHER format here too as a deliberate
# exception -- note why in the commit that adds it.
#
# TODO (deferred, kept as plain SVG for now): these presentation SVGs
# get large -- matplotlib exports every scatter point/CI-band vertex as
# its own full-precision XML path. Fix later: rasterize just the dense
# data layers (ax.scatter(..., rasterized=True), regplot's CI-band
# collection) while keeping text/axes/legends true vector -- smaller
# files, still-crisp labels, no format change needed.
paper/figures/*
!paper/figures/tasks_overview.pdf
!paper/figures/models_overview_paper.pdf
!paper/figures/model_performance.pdf
!paper/figures/lambda_main.pdf
!paper/figures/sigma_main.pdf
!paper/figures/neural_main.pdf
!paper/figures/synaptic_main.pdf

presentations/figures/*
!presentations/figures/temporal_performance.svg
!presentations/figures/model_performance.svg
!presentations/figures/response_change_human.svg
!presentations/figures/response_change_full.svg
!presentations/figures/lambda_human.svg
!presentations/figures/lambda_sanity_human.svg
!presentations/figures/lambda_model_correlation.svg
!presentations/figures/variability_human.svg
!presentations/figures/sigma_sanity_human.svg
!presentations/figures/sigma_model_correlation.svg
!presentations/figures/variance_autocorr_human.svg
!presentations/figures/variance_autocorr_models.svg
!presentations/figures/model_performance_nll.svg
!presentations/figures/PE_dynamics.svg
!presentations/figures/PE_drives_sigma.svg
!presentations/figures/lambda_drives_discounting.svg

